Enhanced Scope of Coverage
Accidental Death Benefit, Double Indemnity Benefit and Medical Reimbursement Benefit shall extend to cover the
following events subject to the terms and conditions of the policy:
a) Strike, Riot and Civil Commotion;
b) Terrorism;
c) Suffocation by Smoke, Poisonous Fumes, Gas and Drowning;
d) Natural Disasters;
e) Disappearance;
f) Hijack, Murder & Assault;
g) Food Poisoning;
h) Insect/ Animal Bites, Stings or Attacks (including dengue fever); and
i) Motor-Cycling.
Retrenchment Benefit
While this policy is in force and provided that there is no premium holiday taken during the premium payment
term, if you are retrenched and remain unemployed for a minimum period of 30 consecutive days from the last
day of service with previous employer
(i) after 24 months of this policy from the issue date, or the last reinstatement date (where applicable);
(ii) prior to the end of premium payment term; and
(iii) before the policy anniversary on which you are Age 70
we will waive future regular premiums payable under the basic policy for up to 12 months. The waiver of premium
will commence from the next premium due date immediately after we receive and approve your application on
Retrenchment Benefit.
Written application for Retrenchment Benefit must be submitted to us within 6 months from the date of
retrenchment.
